arduino-esp32 SD library, vendored and modified in firmware/third_party/SD
  Source: https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32, libraries/SD of core
  2.0.17 (as shipped in PlatformIO framework-arduinoespressif32
  3.20017.241212), copied unchanged except three changes marked "CPA patch"
  in src/sd_diskio.cpp:
    1. the SPI-mode ACMD41 argument carries only HCS (0x40000000 instead of
       0x40100000), so cards that stay idle with the voltage bit initialize;
    2. GET_BLOCK_SIZE reports 8192 sectors (4 MiB) instead of 1, so f_mkfs
       aligns the FAT data area;
    3. the 25 MHz SPI clock cap is skipped only when CPA_SD_UNCAPPED_CLOCK is
       defined (the hardware probes in firmware/hwtest; the app keeps it).
  Copyright 2015-2016 Espressif Systems (Shanghai) PTE LTD
  src/sd_diskio_crc.c: Copyright (c) 2014 Neil Thiessen
  Apache License, Version 2.0 (full text in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)

