4. Visual theme (docs/19-visual-theme.md) - embedded in the firmware image
===============================================================================

WhisperWoof - https://github.com/h3qing/WhisperWoof
The same author's project, MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2026 Heqing Huang (the MIT License text in section 1 applies)
  The colour tokens in tools/theme/tokens.py (and so in
  firmware/app/lib/theme/gen/palette_gen.h) are WhisperWoof's dark theme
  (DESIGN.md, src/index.css .dark) plus REC; ink3 is raised from #8f8276 to
  #96897b. Mando's 15 colours (tools/theme/mando_colours.json; palette entries
  0x20-0x2E and their dimmed copies 0x30-0x3E) are a median cut of every frame
  of website/mando/hd/{wait,think,review,hop}.webp (sha256 in
  mando_colours.json), cropped to their union box, scaled to 64 px and
  composited on #1a1512 by tools/theme/gen_mando.py with Pillow 13.0.0. The
  status bar's 11 x 9 head (firmware/app/lib/theme/gen/icons_gen.h) is
  hand-pixelled in those colours after Mando. Mando's sprites
  (firmware/app/lib/theme/gen/mando46_gen.h and mando64_gen.h) are key poses of
  those same loops - at 46 px frames 0/6/12/18 of wait, review and think, hop
  2/6/10/14 and a dozing frame; at 64 px frames 0/6/12/18 of wait, review and
  think - cropped the same way, scaled with Pillow's Lanczos filter, composited
  on #1a1512, cut to the 15 colours (under 30 % cover is clear) and packed 4 bits
  a pixel; the dozing frame is wait 0 with ten pixels repainted as closed eyes.
  WhisperWoof is only read; the firmware build does not need it
  (tools/theme/README.md).

